ideas/meta-protocol-change-fusion-execplans/round-01/agy.md:40:*   **Rationale:** Currently, `parley-deck` does not track when an agent acts as a "false-alarm blocker" (i.e., raising a `CRITICAL` or `MAJOR` review finding that is subsequently dismissed as invalid). By adapting this concept into the `parley retro` (Section 13) analysis, we can identify agents with high "confident-wrongness" rates to refine their prompts or adjust roster selection.
