ideas/meta-protocol-change-agent-teams-patterns/round-01/claude.md:12:That said, several lower-level Agent Teams habits are genuinely useful and can be borrowed **without** changing PD's core topology: explicit role hints in the participant roster, a context-bundle convention for round-01 isolation, and an explicit allowance for agent-internal subagent use that stays out-of-protocol. I recommend borrowing those three, and explicitly rejecting orchestration, synthesis-by-one-agent, automatic-hook-based phase transitions, and any role mapping that collapses participants into "helpers" of a lead agent.
ideas/meta-protocol-change-agent-teams-patterns/round-01/claude.md:20:   Today the roster in §2 has a single `Role` column that is always `participant`. Borrow the Agent Teams habit of naming a stance (e.g. `planner`, `red-team`, `security-lens`, `perf-lens`, `implementer-candidate`) so participants self-differentiate. Spec change:
